  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Our goal is to write the equation in the form $ax+by=c,$ where $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors and $a\\ge 0.$\n\nWe begin by moving all of the variables to the left-hand side and all of the constants to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-7x-4 \\\\ 7x+y & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors, and $a\\ge 0.$ So we are done!\n\nThe standard form of the line is $7x+y=-4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
